referenceAnswer.en:
Export a matcher config so the proxy only runs on protected routes:
```ts
export const config = {
  matcher: [
    '/((?!login|_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico).*)'
  ]
};
```
This excludes the login page, Next.js internals and static assets from the auth check. Note that in Next.js 16 the file convention is `proxy.ts` with an exported `proxy` function; `middleware.ts` is deprecated.

